# Docs Library

When reading or editing `docs/**`, use this map:

- `docs/adr/` — binding architecture decisions; cite the relevant ADR when proposing structural changes.
- `docs/context/project-memory.md` — phase completion history, deployment IDs, and operational lessons.
- `docs/context/reference-patterns.md` — external repo patterns to reuse.
- `docs/deployment/` — Railway, Open WebUI, Salesforce OAuth, and tenant onboarding runbooks.
- `docs/testing/` — proof docs, UAT checklists, and eval evidence.
- `docs/orchestrator/` — case triage LangGraph node design and contracts.
- `docs/agents/` — agent capability specs and intelligence findings.

When adding docs, match the style of sibling files in the same folder. Do not log secrets, org credentials, or raw PII.

For security or telemetry topics in docs, also follow `.github/instructions/security-observability.instructions.md`.
